,"type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":652,"digest":"sha256:32cc7ec63a50ad675fdd5c056849c30965e208a4aff4b601638a31d0540a1593","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-16T18:31:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T18:31:07Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m124-v0.12.4/m12stage4-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m124-v0.12.4","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m124-v0.12.4","body":"# Engacer OS M12.4 / 0.12.4 — windows and title bars\n\nNative qualification passes **M12-STAGE4-VM-v1** on 16 November 2026.\n[Exact-source acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/69ef51b45794e26df05d0a9a59bde25cdd9a566d/evidence/M12/4/acceptance-results.json) verifies\n576 compiled inputs, fourteen build/ZIP digests, nine native window journeys\nand twelve cached/full comparisons. Public media and complete website proof\nclose separately before M12.5.\n\nBuild: `df69fcb86b63e2ffbd3b821f412f3782`.\nISO SHA256: `3a84ee0d39b1a53bcac2ab3a0469b0bc658655a47c6d7e1c8161e483ffd8a585`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `96a576b3048cb64cbac0319cc47d930042017d40e78656c72f35a0e737f60785`.\n\n## What changes\n\nTitle bars share their drawing, pointer and keyboard geometry. The original app\nicon opens the window menu. Minimize, Maximize/Restore and Close have visible\n36-pixel-high targets, separate hover/press/focus states and measured labels.\nClose uses white artwork on red. Monochrome Maximize/Restore cutouts are truly\ntransparent rather than paper-colored blocks. The existing 57 original icon\nidentities and native Inter remain shared.\n\nActive/inactive windows have distinct captions, borders and title ink. Tab and\nEnter use the same validated caption commands as a click. Normal bounds survive\nmaximize/restore. Existing signed movement, all resize directions, snapping and\nkeyboard window commands remain. The app menu clamps a negative window anchor\nbefore unsigned screen fitting. Selecting the desktop prevents Alt+F4 and\nAlt+Space from targeting a background app. Close preserves the existing unsaved\nreview; file dialogs block their owner rather than the entire desktop.\n\n[How and why](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/69ef51b45794e26df05d0a9a59bde25cdd9a566d/docs/architecture/windows-m124.md),\n[window guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/69ef51b45794e26df05d0a9a59bde25cdd9a566d/docs/handbook/windows-m124.md) and\n[eight-step installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/69ef51b45794e26df05d0a9a59bde25cdd9a566d/docs/handbook/install-m124.md).\n\n## Qualification boundary\n\nThe release requires matching native window journeys, real installation and\nretained-ISO restart, two ordinary disk starts, actual 150% and 4K, exact shipped\nVMware media, separate BIOS journeys and cached/full movement comparisons.\nHost checks cover 53,982,630 geometry points, 384 styles, 731,264 tinted pixels\nand the existing 57-icon geometry/raster oracle. These supplement native observations.\nMemory evidence distinguishes linked shell state, managed pages and configured\nVM RAM. No new per-window framebuffer, raster cache or idle timer is introduced.\n\nThe earlier M12.2 concurrent BIOS/AHCI timeout remains open. Its fresh repeat\npasses, but the trigger is not isolated and stress reliability is unqualified.\nFinal comprehensive regression remains M12.18. Physical hardware, ARM, vendor\nGPU 3D and universal DOS/Windows application compatibility are not qualified by\nthis stage. Agent visual/scenario review is not a human usability study.\n\nLinked fixed desktop BSS/data is **544,212 bytes**, **16 bytes** above M12.3.\nWindow tasks retain zero managed pages and no new allocation failures; idle\nCPUs halt. Inter coverage remains **251,248 bytes**. The icon renderer uses a\n**512-byte transient row**, no raster cache and no new heap allocation.\n[Resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/69ef51b45794e26df05d0a9a59bde25cdd9a566d/evidence/M12/4/resources.json) distinguish these measurements\nfrom configured RAM and total kernel consumption. Observer timings are not FPS.\n\nThe shared window-menu helper footer still uses bounded ellipsis; complete\nfitting is carried to M12.14. Native HiDPI captures motivate a cursor-versus-hit\ncoordinate check in M12.16: caption actions run at the real scale, but scripted\nclicks alone do not qualify pointer usability. Those follow-ups remain explicit\nbefore final M12.18 qualification.\n"}